Maranthorn is a worker in the lower decks of the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]], a tall man the slip has begun to change, with scraggly red and blue feathers in place of hair and the first growth of a beak. He is bound to the strider by a contract held by one of the [[Org/The Harlequins/index|Harlequins]]: a debt that began at two hundred gold and has climbed past eighteen thousand with interest. He wants the surface, and then off the strider altogether.

He knows the lower halls, including the unlit quarter where things that do not belong to the strider are kept. He will take food where he will not take money or wine, which would only get him robbed. [[People/Johnny|Johnny]] arranged to have six sandwiches and a note sent down to him at dawn each day.
